  "summary": "Unified World Models (UWM) use a single diffusion model to learn and predict robot actions and video frames together. This approach helps robots learn better by using both action-labeled data and action-free videos. UWM improves robot policies and generalizes well to new tasks by understanding the link between actions and visual observations.",
